        "dropped the door at (3, 10): a door already occupies the cell, and the first wins",
        "noted a second boundary door at (9, 10): the editor's level carries one entrance, so place any other way in by hand",
        "dropped the door at (4, 7): a door already holds the '4,8:north' edge, and the first wins",
        "the stairs down at (4, 0) carry a fabricated destination (dungeon '', level 2, cell (0, 0), facing north): One Page Dungeon records none, so resolve it against a real level or drop it before publishing",
        "imported 1 portcullis door(s) as locked doors: the editor's door model has no portcullis, so the winch and the see-through grate are lost",
        "imported 1 double door(s) as ordinary doors: the editor's door model has no leaf count",
        "imported 1 barred door(s) as locked doors: the editor's door model cannot say which side the bar is on",
        "imported 1 flight(s) of steps as plain openings: the editor's grid has no intra-level elevation",
        "imported 1 door(s) of unrecognized type 12 as ordinary doors: the format has grown a type this reader predates",
